# Backend Rules

- Read `docs/05-architecture.md`, `docs/06-coding-rules.md`, `docs/07-tech-stack.md`, and `docs/09-ai-rules.md` when relevant.
- Follow existing service, route, server action, and data-access patterns.
- Validate all untrusted external input at system boundaries.
- Keep authorization checks close to protected operations.
- Return explicit, predictable error states; never leak secrets or sensitive internals.
- Keep business logic out of presentation code when an application/service boundary exists.
- Avoid hidden side effects and undocumented global state.
- Add or update tests for changed business behavior.
